    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0529" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v11/pg503"/>

                <head>260. Telegram From the Mission at the United
                        Nations to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d260-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"><placeName>New
                                York</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1957-09-23T17:00:00-04:00">September 23, 1957—5
                            p.m.</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>Delga 33. Verbatim text. Re UN membership. We propose to discuss following draft
                    resolution on membership Vietnam with UKDel
                    and few others with view cosponsorship if Dept
                    has no objections to it.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d260-f2"/> We doubt whether
                    reference to “veto” will have any adverse effects on voting, but if we find
                    opposition in informal discussions would delete it. Res on Korea on which we will consult at same time, would be
                    identical except for substitution of appropriate resolution numbers and
                    “Republic of Korea”.</p>
                <p>The General Assembly</p>
                <p>Recalling its Resolutions 620 C (VII) and 1017 B
                    (XI) finding Vietnam qualified for membership in the United Nations,</p>
                <p>Noting with regret the continued inability of the Security Council to recommend
                    the admission of Vietnam to membership in the United Nations owing to the
                    negative vote of a permanent member of the Security Council,</p>
                <pb facs="0530" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>
                <p>Reaffirms that Vietnam is fully qualified for and should be admitted to
                    membership in the United Nations.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d260-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 310.2/9–2357. Official Use Only.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d260-f2" n="2" xml:id="d260-f2-content">
                <p>The U.N. General Assembly opened its Twelfth Session on September 17.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d260-f3" n="3" xml:id="d260-f3-content">
                <p>Gadel 15 to New York, September 25,
                    authorized the delegation to proceed with the procedure suggested in Delga 33. (Department of State, Central
                    Files, 310.2/ 9–2357)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
